cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the HIM (Cat Intelligence) theory in your research, please cite the works listed below."
title: "HIM-Theory: a reference implementation of Homeostatic Intrinsic Motivation (Cat Intelligence)"
abstract: >-
  Executable reference implementation, baselines and benchmark suite for
  Homeostatic Intrinsic Motivation (HIM) / Cat Intelligence (CI): an autonomous-agent
  architecture driven solely by an internal comfort scalar L and its increment dL,
  with no external reward and no preset goal. Includes a literal transcription of the
  paper's pseudocode (reported as him_v1), an ablation suite, and three baselines
  (free-energy-principle active inference, tabular Q-learning with an external sparse
  reward, and a uniform random walk). The repository also documents, item by item,
  every point where the published text is ambiguous or where the reproduction was
  found to deviate from the numbers reported in the papers.
